  "question": {
    "text": "A Carnot engine operating between temperatures $T_1$ and $T_2$ has efficiency $\\frac{1}{6}$. When $T_2$ is lowered by 62 $\\mathrm{K}$, its efficiency increases to $\\frac{1}{3}$. Then $T_1$ and $T_2$ are, respectively :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "npRjx",
      "text": "\n$372 \\mathrm{~K}$ and $330 \\mathrm{~K}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Tuv51",
      "text": "\n$330 \\mathrm{~K}$ and $268 \\mathrm{~K}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AZcQm",
      "text": "\n$310 \\mathrm{~K}$ and $248 \\mathrm{~K}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2QiHw",
      "text": "\n$372 \\mathrm{~K}$ and $310 \\mathrm{~K}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\eta_1=\\frac{T_1-T_2}{T_1}=\\frac{1}{6}$\n$\\eta_2=\\frac{T_1-\\left(T_2-62\\right)}{T_1}=\\frac{1}{3}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{T_1-T_2}{T_1}+\\frac{62}{T_1}=\\frac{1}{3}$\n$\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{62}{T_1}=\\frac{1}{3}$\n$\\frac{62}{T_1}=\\frac{1}{6}$\n$\\therefore T_1=62 \\times 6=372 \\mathrm{~K}$\n$\\frac{T_1-T_2}{T_1}=\\frac{1}{6}$\n$1-\\frac{T_2}{T_1}=\\frac{1}{6}$\n$\\frac{T_2}{372}=\\frac{5}{6}$\n$\\Rightarrow T_2=310 \\mathrm{~K}$",
    "image": null
  },
